  "coverage": [
    "All nine runtime builds loaded fresh default encounter settings. Another Paper 1.21.11 process started with a pre-existing configuration omitting recipe-book and checked legacy join discovery.",
    "Native item pickup, native client slot clicks, empty clicked slot and renamed custom cursor, raw material lookalikes, shared base material and excluded custom result-only recipe.",
    "Shapeless and shaped recipe input/output rules, furnace input, join-only, manual learning, server-managed virtual anvil exclusion and namespaced recipe keys.",
    "Late cancelled item pickup and inventory click, denied permission, later permission grant, native recipe discovery veto and successful retry, revoked permission on successful live reload.",
    "Previously known encounter-only recipes survived successful catalog reload and real reconnect. Six malformed book definitions failed to publish and retained the active serving catalog.",
    "Eight registered custom ingredients shared IRON_SWORD. The unmarked item and an unrelated registered ID discovered none. Each renamed and damaged matching item unlocked only its own recipe with a server-native discovery event.",
    "Non-air unrelated clicked slot took priority over a custom cursor. The matching cursor placed into an empty slot unlocked the furnace recipe. Other inputs arrived by native player pickup.",
    "Furnace, blasting, smoking, campfire, stonecutting and the template, base and addition inputs of three smithing transforms registered distinct keys and survived actual client reconnect.",
    "The published example YAML and bundled starter loaded together in each isolated core/bundle regression run."
  ],
